IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, s 174 -- the statutory meeting and the statutory report. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- It gives the keel's two inputs for s 4(1) "statutory meeting" and "statutory report" (PLAN.md section 4, table A):
-- `s 174(1) the meeting is the statutory meeting the section requires` and `s 174(2) the report is the statutory report the section requires`.
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4 (P1 to P10, assumed and not ruled). The regulative rules count in days on the trace's clock:
-- time 0 is the day the rule names in its comment, and an act at time n is n days later.
-- The statutory meeting "not less than one month" lower bound cannot be a regulative window on the stable build (AFTER ... WITHIN is rejected), so it
-- sits in the decision function `s 174(1) the statutory meeting is held in the period the subsection fixes`.

§ `Section 174(1): the duty to hold the statutory meeting`

-- src:15662 | 174.—(1) Every public company that is a limited company and has
-- src:15663 | a share capital must, within a period of not less than one month and
-- src:15664 | not more than 3 months after the date at which it is entitled to
-- src:15665 | commence business, hold a general meeting of the members of the
-- src:15666 | company to be called the “statutory meeting”.
@ref s 174(1) (src:15662-15666)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(1) the company must hold a statutory meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the company is a limited company` AND `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every public company that is a limited company and has a share capital must" -- a company outside that description is not under the duty (a duty's own question; marginal reading (a), F-3)

-- The keel's input for s 4(1) "statutory meeting": the meeting is "the meeting mentioned in section 174".
@ref s 174(1) (src:15662-15666)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a general meeting of the members of the company called the statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(1) the meeting is the statutory meeting the section requires` MEANS
    IF `s 174(1) the company must hold a statutory meeting` `the company is a public company` `the company is a limited company` `the company has a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the meeting is a general meeting of the members of the company called the statutory meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hold a general meeting of the members of the company to be called the 'statutory meeting'" -- the meeting is not the general meeting this section requires of such a company

-- "within a period of not less than one month and not more than 3 months after the date at which it is entitled to commence business".
-- The earliest day is one month after (P1, P4); the latest is 3 months after. A period the text fixes in its own words: outside it, JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)).
@ref s 174(1) (src:15662-15666)
GIVEN `the date the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE
      `the date the statutory meeting is held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(1) the statutory meeting is held in the period the subsection fixes` MEANS
    IF    `the date the statutory meeting is held` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company is entitled to commence business` 1 Months)
      AND `the date the statutory meeting is held` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company is entitled to commence business` 3 Months)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a period of not less than one month and not more than 3 months after the date at which it is entitled to commence business" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

GIVEN `the date the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 174(1) the number of days from the date to the last day for the statutory meeting` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company is entitled to commence business` 3 Months) MINUS `the date the company is entitled to commence business`

§ `Section 174(2): the statutory report to every member`

-- src:15668 | (2) The directors must at least 7 days before the day on which the
-- src:15669 | meeting is to be held forward a report to be called the “statutory
-- src:15670 | report” to every member of the company.
@ref s 174(2) (src:15668-15670)
GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors forward the statutory report to every member` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(2) the directors forward the statutory report in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the directors forward the statutory report to every member` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must at least 7 days before the day on which the meeting is to be held forward a report" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes, periods ruling (a))

-- The keel's input for s 4(1) "statutory report": the report is "the report mentioned in section 174".
@ref s 174(2) (src:15668-15670)
GIVEN `the company must hold a statutory meeting under section 174(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is the report that the directors forward to every member of the company for the statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(2) the report is the statutory report the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the company must hold a statutory meeting under section 174(1)` AND `the report is the report that the directors forward to every member of the company for the statutory meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "forward a report to be called the 'statutory report' to every member of the company" -- not the report the directors must forward for the statutory meeting

GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 174(2) the latest day for the directors to forward the statutory report` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` 7 Days

§ `Section 174(3): certified, and what it must state`

-- src:15672 | (3) The statutory report must be certified by not less than 2 directors
-- src:15673 | of the company and must state —
-- src:15678 | (a) the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares
-- src:15679 | allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash,
-- src:15680 | and stating in the case of shares partly paid up the extent to
-- src:15681 | which they are so paid up, and in either case the
-- src:15682 | consideration for which they have been allotted;
-- src:15684 | (b) the total amount of cash received by the company in
-- src:15685 | respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished;
-- src:15687 | (c) an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the
-- src:15688 | payments made thereout up to a date within 7 days of the
-- src:15689 | date of the report exhibiting under distinctive headings the
-- src:15690 | receipts from shares and debentures and other sources the
-- src:15691 | payments made thereout and particulars concerning the
-- src:15692 | balance remaining in hand, and an account or estimate of
-- src:15693 | the preliminary expenses;
-- src:15695 | (d) the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors,
-- src:15696 | trustees for holders of debentures (if any), auditors (if any),
-- src:15697 | chief executive officers (if any) and secretaries of the
-- src:15698 | company; and
-- src:15700 | (e) the particulars of any contract the modification of which is
-- src:15701 | to be submitted to the meeting for its approval together
-- src:15702 | with the particulars of the modification or proposed
-- src:15703 | modification.
@ref s 174(3) (src:15672-15703)
GIVEN `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3) the statutory report is certified by enough directors` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statutory report must be certified by not less than 2 directors of the company" (a duty's own question)

@ref s 174(3)(a) (src:15678-15682)
GIVEN `the report states the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states, in the case of shares partly paid up, the extent to which they are so paid up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states, in either case, the consideration for which the shares have been allotted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(a) the report states the shares allotted` MEANS
    IF    `the report states the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash`
      AND `the report states, in the case of shares partly paid up, the extent to which they are so paid up`
      AND `the report states, in either case, the consideration for which the shares have been allotted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state (a) the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing ...; and stating in the case of shares partly paid up the extent ..., and in either case the consideration" (a duty's own question)

@ref s 174(3)(b) (src:15684-15685)
GIVEN `the report states the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(b) the report states the cash received` MEANS
    IF `the report states the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state (b) the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished" (a duty's own question)

-- (c) "an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report". "Within 7 days of" is read
-- both ways (7 days before to 7 days after the date of the report); the other reading, 7 days before only, is fork line F-4.
@ref s 174(3)(c) (src:15687-15693)
GIVEN `the date up to which the abstract of receipts and payments is made up` IS A DATE
      `the date of the statutory report` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(c) the abstract is made up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report` MEANS
    IF    `the date up to which the abstract of receipts and payments is made up` AT LEAST (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the statutory report` 7 Days)
      AND `the date up to which the abstract of receipts and payments is made up` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the statutory report` 7 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report" (a period the text fixes; F-4)

@ref s 174(3)(c) (src:15687-15693)
GIVEN `the report contains an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abstract is made up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abstract exhibits under distinctive headings the receipts from shares and debentures and other sources, the payments made thereout and particulars concerning the balance remaining in hand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(c) the report states the abstract and the account` MEANS
    IF    `the report contains an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout`
      AND `the abstract is made up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report`
      AND `the abstract exhibits under distinctive headings the receipts from shares and debentures and other sources, the payments made thereout and particulars concerning the balance remaining in hand`
      AND `the report contains an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state (c) an abstract of the receipts ... exhibiting under distinctive headings ... and an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses" (a duty's own question)

@ref s 174(3)(d) (src:15695-15698)
GIVEN `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has trustees for holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the trustees for holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(d) the report states the names and addresses and descriptions` MEANS
    IF    `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors`
      AND ((NOT `the company has trustees for holders of debentures`) OR `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the trustees for holders of debentures`)
      AND ((NOT `the company has auditors`) OR `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the auditors`)
      AND ((NOT `the company has chief executive officers`) OR `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the chief executive officers`)
      AND `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the secretaries of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state (d) the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors, trustees for holders of debentures (if any), auditors (if any), chief executive officers (if any) and secretaries of the company" (a duty's own question)

@ref s 174(3)(e) (src:15700-15703)
GIVEN `a contract the modification of which is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the particulars of the contract together with the particulars of the modification or proposed modification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3)(e) the report states the particulars of the contract` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a contract the modification of which is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval exists`) OR `the report states the particulars of the contract together with the particulars of the modification or proposed modification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state (e) the particulars of any contract the modification of which is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval together with the particulars of the modification" (a duty's own question; with no such contract nothing is required, F-5)

-- (3) as a whole: certified by not less than 2 directors and stating (a) to (e).
@ref s 174(3) (src:15672-15703)
GIVEN `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` IS A NUMBER
      a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      d IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      e IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3) the statutory report is certified and states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `s 174(3) the statutory report is certified by enough directors` `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND b EQUALS JUST TRUE AND c EQUALS JUST TRUE AND d EQUALS JUST TRUE AND e EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be certified by not less than 2 directors of the company and must state (a) ... (e)" (a duty's own question)

§ `Section 174(4) to (6): the auditors, the Registrar and the list of members`

-- (4): "by the auditors, if any". With no auditors nothing is required, so the requirement is met vacuously (F-6).
-- src:15707 | (4) The statutory report must, so far as it relates to the shares
-- src:15708 | allotted and to the cash received in respect of such shares and to the
-- src:15709 | receipts and payments on capital account, be examined and reported
-- src:15710 | upon by the auditors, if any.
@ref s 174(4) (src:15707-15710)
GIVEN `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditors have examined the statutory report so far as it relates to the shares allotted, the cash received in respect of such shares and the receipts and payments on capital account, and reported upon it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(4) the statutory report has been examined and reported upon by the auditors` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has auditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- no auditors: "by the auditors, if any" -- nothing is required of a company with none (F-6)
    ELSE (IF `the auditors have examined the statutory report so far as it relates to the shares allotted, the cash received in respect of such shares and the receipts and payments on capital account, and reported upon it`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statutory report must, so far as it relates to the shares allotted ..., be examined and reported upon by the auditors, if any" (a duty's own question)

-- src:15712 | (5) The directors must cause a copy of the statutory report and the
-- src:15713 | auditor’s report (if any) to be lodged with the Registrar at least 7 days
-- src:15714 | before the date of the statutory meeting.
@ref s 174(5) (src:15712-15714)
GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy of the statutory report and of the auditor's report is lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(5) the copy has been lodged with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the copy of the statutory report and of the auditor's report is lodged with the Registrar` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must cause a copy of the statutory report and the auditor's report (if any) to be lodged with the Registrar at least 7 days before the date of the statutory meeting" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 174(5) the latest day for the directors to cause the copy to be lodged` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` 7 Days

-- src:15716 | (6) The directors must cause a list showing the names and addresses
-- src:15717 | of the members and the number of shares held by them respectively to
-- src:15718 | be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open
-- src:15719 | and accessible to any member during the continuance of the meeting.
@ref s 174(6) (src:15716-15719)
GIVEN `the list showing the names and addresses of the members and the number of shares held by them respectively was produced at the commencement of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list remained open and accessible to any member during the continuance of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(6) the list of members has been produced and kept open and accessible` MEANS
    IF `the list showing the names and addresses of the members and the number of shares held by them respectively was produced at the commencement of the meeting` AND `the list remained open and accessible to any member during the continuance of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must cause a list ... to be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open and accessible to any member during the continuance of the meeting" (a duty's own question)

§ `Section 174(7) to (9): what the meeting may do`

-- (7): the members present "are at liberty to discuss any matter relating to the formation of the company or arising out of the statutory report, whether previous notice
-- has been given or not". A liberty limited by its own wording: a matter outside it is NOT the text's no, so NOTHING.
-- src:15724 | (7) The members present at the meeting are at liberty to discuss any
-- src:15725 | matter relating to the formation of the company or arising out of the
-- src:15726 | statutory report, whether previous notice has been given or not, but no
-- src:15727 | resolution of which notice has not been given in accordance with the
-- src:15728 | constitution may be passed.
@ref s 174(7) (src:15724-15728)
GIVEN `the matter relates to the formation of the company or arises out of the statutory report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(7) the members present are at liberty to discuss the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter relates to the formation of the company or arises out of the statutory report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at liberty to discuss any matter relating to the formation of the company or arising out of the statutory report" -- a matter of neither kind is outside the liberty, which the text does not forbid or grant

-- (7) second limb: "no resolution of which notice has not been given in accordance with the constitution may be passed" -- a bar. JUST TRUE = barred.
@ref s 174(7) (src:15724-15728)
GIVEN `notice of the resolution has been given in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(7) the resolution is barred because notice has not been given in accordance with the constitution` MEANS
    IF `notice of the resolution has been given in accordance with the constitution`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no resolution of which notice has not been given in accordance with the constitution may be passed" -- notice was given, so this bar does not apply (a bar's own question)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (8): "at any adjourned meeting any resolution of which notice has been given in accordance with the constitution either before or subsequently to the former meeting may be passed".
-- src:15732 | (8) The meeting may adjourn from time to time and at any
-- src:15733 | adjourned meeting any resolution of which notice has been given in
-- src:15734 | accordance with the constitution either before or subsequently to the
-- src:15735 | former meeting may be passed and the adjourned meeting has the
-- src:15736 | same powers as an original meeting.
@ref s 174(8) (src:15732-15736)
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the resolution has been given in accordance with the constitution either before or subsequently to the former meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(8) a resolution may be passed at the adjourned meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting` AND `notice of the resolution has been given in accordance with the constitution either before or subsequently to the former meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any resolution of which notice has been given in accordance with the constitution either before or subsequently to the former meeting may be passed" -- a grant limited by its own wording (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; F-7)

@ref s 174(8) (src:15732-15736)
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(8) the adjourned meeting has the same powers as an original meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the adjourned meeting" of the statutory meeting only

-- src:15740 | (9) The meeting may by ordinary resolution appoint a committee or
-- src:15741 | committees of inquiry, and at any adjourned meeting a special
-- src:15742 | resolution may be passed that the company be wound up if, despite
-- src:15743 | any other provision of this Act, at least 7 days’ notice of intention to
-- src:15744 | propose the resolution has been given to every member of the
-- src:15745 | company.
@ref s 174(9) (src:15740-15745)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of resolution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(9) the meeting may appoint a committee of inquiry by the resolution` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `an ordinary resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The meeting may by ordinary resolution appoint a committee or committees of inquiry" -- by another kind of resolution the grant is not given (F-8)

-- (9) second limb: "at any adjourned meeting a special resolution may be passed that the company be wound up if, despite any other provision of this Act, at least 7 days' notice of intention to
-- propose the resolution has been given to every member of the company". A grant with an "if" gate: when the gate fails, NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1; F-9).
@ref s 174(9) (src:15740-15745)
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a special resolution that the company be wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date notice of intention to propose the resolution was given to the last member of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(9) a special resolution that the company be wound up may be passed at the adjourned meeting` MEANS
    IF    `the meeting is an adjourned statutory meeting` AND `the resolution is a special resolution that the company be wound up`
      AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date notice of intention to propose the resolution was given to the last member of the company` `the date of the adjourned meeting` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a special resolution may be passed that the company be wound up if, despite any other provision of this Act, at least 7 days' notice ... has been given to every member" (grant with an "if" gate, F-9)

§ `Section 174(10): the offence`

-- src:15747 | (10) In the event of any default in complying with this section every
-- src:15748 | officer of the company who is in default and every director of the
-- src:15749 | company who fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance
-- src:15750 | with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:15751 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default
-- src:15752 | penalty.
@ref s 174(10) (src:15747-15752)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance with section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with section 174` AND (`the person is an officer of the company who is in default` OR `the person is a director of the company who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance with section 174`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "In the event of any default in complying with this section every officer of the company who is in default and every director of the company who fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance with this section shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 174(10) (src:15747-15752)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance with section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 174(10) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 174(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the company has made default in complying with section 174` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` `the person is a director of the company who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance with section 174` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of s 174(1), (2), (5) and (6)`

DECLARE `s 174 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 174(1) hold the statutory meeting`
    `s 174(2) forward the statutory report to every member`
    `s 174(5) lodge a copy of the statutory report and the auditor's report with the Registrar`
    `s 174(6) cause the list of members to be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open and accessible to any member during the meeting`

-- The clock: time 0 is the date the company is entitled to commence business; the deadline is the last day of the 3 months after it (the "not less than one month" edge is in the decision function).
-- src:15662 | 174.—(1) Every public company that is a limited company and has
-- src:15663 | a share capital must, within a period of not less than one month and
-- src:15664 | not more than 3 months after the date at which it is entitled to
-- src:15665 | commence business, hold a general meeting of the members of the
-- src:15666 | company to be called the “statutory meeting”.
@ref s 174(1) (src:15662-15666)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the date the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 174 act`
`s 174(1) the company must hold the statutory meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 174(1) hold the statutory meeting`
    WITHIN (`s 174(1) the number of days from the date to the last day for the statutory meeting` `the date the company is entitled to commence business`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not hold the statutory meeting within 3 months after the date at which it was entitled to commence business"

-- The clock: time 0 is the day the directors start (the day the rule is entered); the deadline is the latest day, 7 days before the meeting.
-- src:15668 | (2) The directors must at least 7 days before the day on which the
-- src:15669 | meeting is to be held forward a report to be called the “statutory
-- src:15670 | report” to every member of the company.
@ref s 174(2) (src:15668-15670)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
      `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 174 act`
`s 174(2) the directors must forward the statutory report` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 174(2) forward the statutory report to every member`
    WITHIN (`s 174(2) the latest day for the directors to forward the statutory report` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` MINUS `the day the clock starts`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not forward the statutory report to every member at least 7 days before the day of the meeting"

-- src:15712 | (5) The directors must cause a copy of the statutory report and the
-- src:15713 | auditor’s report (if any) to be lodged with the Registrar at least 7 days
-- src:15714 | before the date of the statutory meeting.
@ref s 174(5) (src:15712-15714)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
      `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 174 act`
`s 174(5) the directors must cause the copy to be lodged` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 174(5) lodge a copy of the statutory report and the auditor's report with the Registrar`
    WITHIN (`s 174(5) the latest day for the directors to cause the copy to be lodged` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` MINUS `the day the clock starts`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not cause a copy of the statutory report and the auditor's report to be lodged with the Registrar at least 7 days before the date of the statutory meeting"

-- s 174(6): "at the commencement of the meeting" is a moment of the meeting, not a period counted from an event of this rule, and no consequence is stated in the subsection:
-- the rule has no WITHIN, so a late act still reads FULFILLED and no trace can reach BREACH (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:15716 | (6) The directors must cause a list showing the names and addresses
-- src:15717 | of the members and the number of shares held by them respectively to
-- src:15718 | be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open
-- src:15719 | and accessible to any member during the continuance of the meeting.
@ref s 174(6) (src:15716-15719)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 174 act`
`s 174(6) the directors must cause the list of members to be produced and kept open and accessible (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 174(6) cause the list of members to be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open and accessible to any member during the meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not cause the list of members to be produced at the commencement of the meeting and to remain open and accessible to any member during the meeting" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
